The Negotiator — Cleaning Vertical · 5h Build Plan (v4 · three-agent)
Team: Nirma (frontend) · Umra (backend core) · Aleks (intake backend + conversation design + EL dashboard + personas) · Maxim (voice integration + negotiation loop) Stack: FastAPI (Python) · Supabase · React + Tailwind · ElevenLabs Agents · Claude Code Clock: Build 22:00–03:00 CET tonight · sleep · 10:30–13:00 CET demo recording + submission (deadline 15:00, keep 2h buffer)


Locked decisions
Vertical: home cleaning. The demo generates the price spread live: one confirmed spec, three quotes 2–3x apart.
Counterparties: Aleks role-plays all 3 personas on live web calls, back-to-back, from persona cards.
Voice interview: live-interactive on the recording — the intake agent actually works; the demo shows real unscripted interaction with it.
Three agents, three jobs: Agent 1 Interviewer (1-on-1 intake with the user) · Agent 2 Caller (calls providers, shares the spec, collects first quotes) · Agent 3 Closer (renegotiates using real competing bids). Maps 1:1 to the brief's Estimator/Caller/Closer modules; demo runs two call rounds.
Text-first. Full loop runs in text by 00:30 (guaranteed submission); voice snaps on after.
Ownership rule: all intake writes go through Aleks's endpoints. POST /intake/doc and POST /specs are Aleks's — one person owns doc/interview → spec JSON → DB. Everyone else consumes, never writes, specs.
Honesty guardrail (everyone): the agent may cite a real competing quote from the DB; it may never invent a bid, inventory, or scope. Scored criterion.
Screen 3 updates after each call completes — no streaming; frontend polls and flips cards on call end.


